From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:21:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: add raw FEL composition HDR10 output

HDR10 Rendering always runs libplacebo's spline tone mapper and
perceptual gamut mapper against the static L6/source-max target. Some
displays should instead receive the reconstructed BL+EL picture
untouched and do their own mapping, the way native HDR10 is handled.

Add a raw variant of the Basic HDR10 session. It reuses the same
validation, FEL pairing and transport, but renders into a target that
is identical to the reconstructed source colour space with clip
mappers, so no tone or gamut mapping runs and no post-scale ceiling
is applied below PQ 1.0. Because the output is the source signal,
L6 MaxCLL/MaxFALL and the mastering black level are carried as-is
instead of being reported unknown.

Selection is a policy flag on DVBRIDGE_MODE_HDR10_BASIC, so admission,
link-depth and HDMI handling stay shared with Basic.
